  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "If \\(|x - 2| = p,\\) where \\(x \\lt 2,\\) then what is \\(x - p?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-2\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(2 - 2p\\)",
    "D": "\\(2p - 2\\)",
    "E": "\\(|2p - 2|\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The condition \\(x<2\\) tells us that \\(x-2<0\\). The absolute value of a negative number is its opposite, so\n\\[\np=|x-2|=-(x-2)=2-x>0.\n\\]\nRearranging gives \\(x=2-p\\). Substituting this into the requested expression yields\n\\[\nx-p=(2-p)-p=\\boxed{2-2p}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
